// JUnit 5 + AssertJ — verifies one rule per test, in isolation
class DiscountServiceTest {
    private final DiscountService service = new DiscountService();

    @Test
    void shouldApply10PercentDiscountForPremiumCustomers() {
        // Arrange
        var customer = new Customer("C123", CustomerTier.PREMIUM);
        var order = new Order(100.0);
        // Act
        double finalPrice = service.calculateFinalPrice(order, customer);
        // Assert
        assertThat(finalPrice).isEqualTo(90.0); // 10% off applied
    }

    @Test
    void shouldNotApplyDiscountForRegularCustomers() {
        var customer = new Customer("C456", CustomerTier.REGULAR);
        double finalPrice = service.calculateFinalPrice(new Order(100.0), customer);
        assertThat(finalPrice).isEqualTo(100.0); // no discount
    }
}
```
Each test names the scenario, exercises one path, and asserts the observable result — so a failure points straight at the broken rule.

